Subject: [PATCH 1/2] MANARA-BACKEND-SQLITE-WAL-FIX-01: make WAL sidecar probe
 test idempotent
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Reproduced in fresh workspace after c6a7edb. Original local commit was
3b34a5a in the previous workspace but was never pushed to origin/main
(no GitHub push credentials were available in that sandbox). This commit
applies the same minimal verified fix to the freshly-cloned tree.

Root cause: test_wal_sidecar_files_created_after_write inserts id=1 into
a probe table that is NOT dropped by conftest between test runs. On the
second run the existing row causes:

    sqlalchemy.exc.IntegrityError: UNIQUE constraint failed: _wal_probe.id

Switch INSERT -> INSERT OR REPLACE so the test is idempotent across
runs. The probe table contents are irrelevant to the assertion (which
only checks for the existence of -wal / -shm sidecar files after a
write), so this change does not weaken the test.

This is the second commit on top of c6a7edb. It is local-only — push
requires owner-provided credentials or a CI workflow with write access.
