Diagnosed UI-02 with REAL Vite + FastAPI + Playwright (no sandbox
substitute, no fixtures). Found three independent defects that
collectively blocked UI-02, none of which had anything to do with
lucide-react packaging (which the previous session mis-diagnosed):

1. CoverageLevel case mismatch (api-client.ts):
   The backend CoverageLevel enum emits lowercase values
   ('none', 'catalog', 'operational', 'verified'). The frontend
   CoverageLevel type expects uppercase
   ('NONE', 'CATALOG', 'OPERATIONAL', 'VERIFIED').
   Without normalization, CoverageBadge crashes with:
     'Cannot read properties of undefined (reading bg)'
   because COVERAGE_STYLES['none'] is undefined. The crash
   propagates up through GapRow -> ComposeResult -> ManaraShell,
   leaving the page blank after compose.
   Fix: normalize coverage_level on the API boundary in compose().
   Unknown values default to 'NONE' (honest 'no coverage').

2. CoverageBadge defensive fallback (Badges.tsx):
   Make CoverageBadge resilient to unexpected coverage_level values.
   Previously, a single bad value took down the whole ComposeResult
   subtree (no error boundary). Now it falls back to NONE styles
   with a sensible label.

3. Workflow lazy-initialization on 404 (InvestigationWorkspace.tsx):
   The backend creates a workflow row lazily (on first transition),
   not at compose time. So GET /mold-factory/investigations/{id}/workflow
   returns 404 immediately after a fresh compose. The frontend
   previously showed a 'Request to /workflow failed with HTTP 404'
   error state instead of initializing the workflow.
   Fix: on 404, POST to /workflow to initialize (the endpoint exists
   for this purpose — confirmed at mold_factory.py:479-501), then
   re-fetch. Other errors still surface honestly.

